Every opioid-dosage-reduction-decision is an opioid-dosage-management-decision.
Every opioid-dosage-continuation-decision is an opioid-dosage-management-decision.
Every evidence-based-medication-treatment-offer is an opioid-use-disorder-medication-treatment-action.
Every patient-referral-for-medication-treatment is an opioid-use-disorder-medication-treatment-action.
If a patient has an unexpected-toxicology-result then every clinician should optimize a pain-management-strategy for the patient.
If a patient has an unexpected-toxicology-result then every clinician should weigh a benefit against a risk during an opioid-dosage-management-decision for the patient.
If a patient has an unexpected-toxicology-result then every clinician should increase a follow-up-frequency for the patient.
If a patient has an unexpected-toxicology-result then every clinician should offer a naloxone-dose to the patient.
If a patient has an unexpected-toxicology-result then every clinician should conduct an opioid-use-disorder-medication-treatment-action for the patient.
